{
  "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
  "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Supreme Court of the United States",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:01 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Travelers Casualty and Surety Company",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Ninth Circuit's Fobian rule creates an unwarranted Federal common law rule that exists outside the structure of the Bankruptcy Code."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Can you tell me -- this is just basic bankruptcy. I should know, but I looked it up and couldn't find it. A standard promissory note which provides for attorneys' fees, the holder of the note is the creditor, the maker of the note is the bankrupt -- the maker of the note goes bankrupt. The holder of the note gets his attorney and says: File a claim in bankruptcy. And the attorney sends him a bill. Is the attorneys' fees, the attorney fee for filing the bankruptcy claim, recoverable as part of the claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Travelers Casualty and Surety Company",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Any right to payment, literally any right to payment, when the debtor files for bankruptcy, that becomes a claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Could you just back up just for a second? Supposing at the time of the bankruptcy that the services have not been performed. It's post-petition conduct by the lawyer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Travelers Casualty and Surety Company",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The problem, Justice Ginsburg, is that the plan said nothing at all. And when the plan says nothing at all, the default rule in bankruptcy is that rights are extinguished; they are discharged under Section 1141(d)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Let me just ask you about the Fobian, and I know Justice Breyer has a question. Let's assume that you're correct in that the fees are allowable. Can the bankruptcy court make the determination of the reasonableness of the fees?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In our brief, we cite to many, many cases in which attorneys' fees are allowed as unsecured claims."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: But what I don't -- there is a body of law on the other side of that issue, too, isn't there?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But it would be proper to remand for the Ninth Circuit to consider those other arguments?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We do not, Your Honor. The Fobian rule is wrong at least, especially as to the distinction that it draws between State law and Federal litigation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0001-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is an enormous amount of affirmative harm that can come from this Court simply saying, let us conclude that the Ninth Circuit was wrong in disallowing these claims on the logic that the Ninth Circuit followed, but we will reserve for a later day an open question of law on what Section 502(b) and 506(b) means."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Which are those two?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Travelers",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Travelers cites -- and I apologize it's not in any of the appendices -- 502(b)(4). And 502(b)(4) underscores our point. 502(b)(4) says, and I'm quoting directly from the code: \"A claim is allowed to the\" -- \"is disallowed to the extent that,\" and then \"(4) if such claim is for services of an insider or attorney and such claim exceeds the reasonable value of such services.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: If you prevail, why can't every attorney who represents a creditor who has a credit card or a promissory note providing for attorneys' fees file something in bankruptcy and get"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Brunstad",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BRUNSTAD: That already happens, Justice Kennedy. In all the circuits that recognize that attorneys' fees are allowed as unsecured claims, that already happens. And that has not cause any disaster or any problem. It's been a practice for 100 years. If Congress had wished to change the practice, it would have when it codified the Bankruptcy Code in 1979. The fact that it hasn't perceived it to be a problem demonstrates that Congress wanted to leave the practice unchanged."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: It's interesting. You're of course a teacher too. The amicus brief by a bunch of professors has a different view of the history than you're describing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Would you say a word about Justice Holmes' opinion in the Scruggs case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1429",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8da5c9934ad25410b10c15b2235977ba1a56370776dd31d46e1e10919cb61033",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8da5c9934ad2-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
